tch_bm":0.6525,"secs":1,"replay":null},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-18 13:28:27","label":"z1 iteration 125","note":"","policy":"runs/z1/net_125.npy","n":1000,"score":0.6365,"ci":[0.6062,0.6657],"big_money":0.88,"smithy_bm":0.705,"witch_bm":0.6475,"secs":1,"replay":null},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-18 13:26:15","label":"z1 iteration 100","note":"","policy":"runs/z1/net_100.npy","n":1000,"score":0.642,"ci":[0.6118,0.6711],"big_money":0.8575,"smithy_bm":0.6975,"witch_bm":0.6825,"secs":112,"vs_az":0.4935,"vs_az_ci":[0.4626,0.5245],"vs_az_n":1000,"replay":null},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-18 13:21:59","label":"z1 iteration 75","note":"","policy":"runs/z1/net_75.npy","n":1000,"score":0.6285,"ci":[0.5981,0.6579],"big_money":0.8575,"smithy_bm":0.6625,"witch_bm":0.6625,"secs":1,"replay":null},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-18 13:18:26","label":"z1 iteration 50","note":"","policy":"runs/z1/net_50.npy","n":1000,"score":0.585,"ci":[0.5542,0.6152],"big_money":0.8575,"smithy_bm":0.65,"witch_bm":0.5925,"secs":2,"replay":null},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Start from random weights, no imitation","text":"rl-v2 tests whether the GA genome is a head start or a ceiling: same network, inputs and PPO as rl-v1, only the start changes. Self-play first, then the bots, then every earlier model.","rejected":"Imitation first (that is rl-v1); a new architecture (would mix two changes into one comparison)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Stage 1 ends on a plateau, not a score","text":"The first start ended self-play after 12 iterations, when it beat the bots 50% of the time. Self-play is the point of the project, so stage 1 now runs until the score against the GA genome has not improved for 60 iterations (at most 400): it shows how far self-play gets alone.","rejected":"A fixed bots threshold (ended the stage after 3 minutes); a fixed iteration count (could stop while it is still learning, or waste hours on a plateau)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"1,500 games per iteration","text":"Random players make long games with ~210 decisions each; 3,000 of them (rl-v1's setting) ran the 8 GB laptop out of memory. 1,500 fit with room for the evaluation.","rejected":"Keeping 3,000 with float16 features (a change to the shared code that rl-v1 does not have)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Same evaluation games as rl-v1","text":"The per-iteration evaluation and the goal checks use rl-v1's and az-v1's seeds, so every number compares directly with them. A new confirmation seed is kept for the end.","rejected":"New evaluation seeds (no direct comparison)."},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-18 13:15:21","label":"z1 iteration 25","note":"","policy":"runs/z1/net_25.npy","n":1000,"score":0.5085,"ci":[0.4775,0.5394],"big_money":0.76,"smithy_bm":0.53,"witch_bm":0.495,"secs":1,"replay":null}]